  "id": "DrugBank_DB06290 - MONDO_5354",
  "verbalization": "Simeprevir is associated with Chronic Hepatitis C Virus Infection through a series of indirect pathways, all of which involve the treatment of Hepatitis C Virus Infection. The drug is indicated for Hepatitis C Virus Infection, and this indication is linked to two other drugs—Pibrentasvir, Beclabuvir, and Elbasvir—that are also indicated for the same condition. These drugs are part of a class of antiviral medications used in the management of Hepatitis C Virus Infection, suggesting a shared mechanism of action. The evidence suggests that Simeprevir may be repurposed for the treatment of Chronic Hepatitis C Virus Infection, as it shares a common indication with other drugs that are used in this context. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Simeprevir to be used in the treatment of Chronic Hepatitis C Virus Infection, based on its relationship with the condition through a chain of indications.",
